# 7. Structured intent schema

Use structured output for routing. Do not parse free-form model text to decide whether an action is safe.

```json
{
  "intent": "order|reorder|recommend|track_order|complaint|campaign_reply|opt_out|support|unknown",
  "language": "ar-LB|en|arabizi|mixed|unknown",
  "confidence": 0.0,
  "entities": {
    "restaurant_name": null,
    "item_names": [],
    "quantities": [],
    "modifiers": [],
    "village": null,
    "delivery_time": null,
    "budget_usd": null,
    "diet_or_allergy_statement": null,
    "campaign_id": null
  },
  "needs_clarification": false,
  "clarification_question": null,
  "risk_flags": [],
  "recommended_next_action": "answer|tool_call|ask|confirm|handoff"
}
```

Validation rules:

- `confidence` is advisory only; the backend may require clarification regardless of confidence.
- `risk_flags` must be checked by deterministic code.
- The model cannot set consent, payment, order status, or campaign eligibility through this schema.

