# 13. Claude and OpenAI provider adapter

Keep provider-specific code behind one interface:

```ts
interface AloKingModelProvider {
  runStructured<T>(request: {
    system: string;
    developer?: string;
    input: unknown;
    tools: ToolDefinition[];
    schema: JsonSchema;
    model: string;
    temperature?: number;
  }): Promise<T>;

  runResponse(request: {
    system: string;
    developer?: string;
    input: unknown;
    tools: ToolDefinition[];
    model: string;
  }): Promise<ModelResponse>;
}
```

The application should not contain separate business logic such as:

```text
if Claude then use one campaign rule
if OpenAI then use another campaign rule
```

Provider differences should be limited to:

- request serialization;
- tool-call parsing;
- structured-output handling;
- retry/error mapping;
- model selection;
- token and latency metrics.

Use a deterministic fallback when the model is unavailable:

```text
exact reorder
→ popular available item
→ approved campaign offer
→ human handoff
```

Never fall back to an unvalidated free-form answer for price or availability.

